      "writtenOn": "2019-01-11T20:48:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interestingly, HIDL now supports the safe_union type, which is exactly a discriminated union.  I\u0027m not sure how deep the changes required to use it would go (deep, I suspect), but it may be worth a try. I guess you can\u0027t just extend a struct, right?\n\nAll of these issues argue for inserting the CertificationLevel somewhere else in the attestation schema, rather than adding it to the authorization list.  Probably in the KeyDescription SEQUENCE (see https://developer.android.com/training/articles/security-key-attestation).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 32,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "83c8a01b3aa08a4e3817b456d766c3f04c575729",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
